{
  "summary": "The multimodal, multiprofile scVI_n200 + ResNet50 configuration with avgpool and concat achieved validation accuracy 0.6315 and F1 0.6068, slightly below the prior RNA-only scVI_n200 avgpool baseline of 0.6501 accuracy and 0.6275 F1. This initial observation suggests that adding ResNet50 image features with simple concat did not improve validation performance over the strongest RNA multiprofile setting, though the comparison does not isolate whether the image modality, concat fusion, or their interaction is responsible. It remains uncertain whether this reflects limited complementary image signal, an inadequate image encoder or fusion design, or uncontrolled variability, so further multimodal exploration should be treated as unresolved."
}

